@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Create documents" ;
    dct:description "Learn how to create container and item documents" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .
    
<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">Learn how to create container and item documents</p>
    <p class="text-center">
        <iframe allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen" frameborder="0" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/paetjTkFBxE" width="560"></iframe>
    </p>
    <p>To create a container document (which can have <a href="../../../reference/data-model/documents/#hierarchy" target="_blank">children documents</a>) with a custom URL, follow these steps:</p>
    <div class="tabbable">
        <ul class="nav nav-tabs">
            <li class="active"><a>User interface</a></li>
            <li><a>Command line interface</a></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tab-content">
            <div class="tab-pane active">
                <div>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Click the <span class="btn btn-primary create-action">Create <span class="caret"></span></span> dropdown in the top-left corner and select <dfn>Container</dfn>. This will open a new form.</li>
                        <li>Fill out the mandatory <dfn>Container</dfn> fields in the form:
                            <dl>
                                <dt>Title</dt>
                                <dd>Enter <samp>Categories</samp></dd>
                            </dl>
                        </li>
                        <li>To customize the container URL, click on the dropdown in the top-right corner of the form</li>
                        <li>Replace the generated unique relative URI with <samp>categories</samp></li>
                        <li>Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span></li>
                    </ol>
                    <p>See how below:</p>
                    <p>
                        <object data="../../../uploads/490945931415b9ab201ed85f296a84c8a11134d1" type="video/webm"></object>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tab-pane">
                <div>
                    <p>With the <a href="../../../reference/command-line-interface/#environment-variables"><samp>LDH_*</samp> environment variables</a> supplying the certificate and base URI, execute the following command:</p>
                    <pre>ldh create-container \\
  --title "Categories" \\
  --slug "categories" \\
  --parent "$LDH_BASE"</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p>A container titled <samp>Categories</samp> should appear with the URI <a href="https://localhost:4443/categories/" target="_blank">https://localhost:4443/categories/</a>.</p>
    <div>
        <h2 id="create-item">Create an item</h2>
        <p>Items are created the same way — select <dfn>Item</dfn> from the <span class="btn btn-primary create-action">Create <span class="caret"></span></span> dropdown instead, or from the command line:</p>
        <pre>ldh create-item \\
  --container "https://localhost:4443/categories/" \\
  --title "Beverages" \\
  --slug "1"</pre>
        <p>The command prints the created document's URL — <samp>https://localhost:4443/categories/1/</samp>.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="lead"><a href="../../../reference/data-model/documents/" target="_blank">Read more about document management.</a></p>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .